# Communication Language

<!-- Single source of truth for communication language settings.
     Changing the values below affects the entire rule set. -->

## Active Settings

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| `<communication-language>` | Czech (čeština) |
| `<lang-code>` | `cs` |

## Rules Derived from This Setting

- **Chat with the user**: always in `<communication-language>`, unless the user writes otherwise.
- **Language of rules and skills**: always **English**. Do not add translation comments or a second-language copy of the rule or skill text.
- **Language of code**: identifiers, docstrings, inline comments, and commit messages are always **English**.
- **Run prose for the Human** (`report.md`, `review.md`, `status.md`, and similar): write in `<communication-language>`. Intent nodes are always English.

## How to Change the Communication Language

Edit only this file — change `<communication-language>` and `<lang-code>` in the table above.
All other rules read the setting from here. Changing this table affects chat and Human-facing run documents; it does not require translating `.mdc` or `SKILL.md` files.

| Language | `<communication-language>` | `<lang-code>` |
|----------|---------------------------|---------------|
| Czech | Czech (čeština) | `cs` |
| German | German (Deutsch) | `de` |
| English | English | `en` |
